{"id": 4424415, "name": "JAMES v. NORTHWESTERN RAILROAD CO.", "name_abbreviation": "James v. Northwestern Railroad", "decision_date": "1905-03-04", "docket_number": "", "first_page": "554", "last_page": "555", "citations": [{"type": "official", "cite": "70 S.C. 554"}], "court": {"name_abbreviation": "S.C.", "id": 8894, "name": "Supreme Court of South Carolina"}, "jurisdiction": {"id": 59, "name_long": "South Carolina", "name": "S.C."}, "cites_to": [], "analysis": {"cardinality": 95, "char_count": 1135, "ocr_confidence": 0.566, "pagerank": {"raw": 1.066067593523183e-07, "percentile": 0.5583985784499406}, "sha256": "bb32dd1eddd336780569c0e5cde0b95e0a28d5c27086fe5d89aca53f35225b1f", "simhash": "1:ce1c5788ae85df99", "word_count": 182}, "last_updated": "2023-07-14T18:56:42.209804+00:00", "provenance": {"date_added": "2019-08-29", "source": "Harvard", "batch": "2018"}, "casebody": {"judges": [], "parties": ["JAMES v. NORTHWESTERN RAILROAD CO."], "opinions": [{"text": "The opinion of the Court was delivered by\nMr. Justice Woods.\nThe plaintiff recovered judgment in a magistrate court for twenty-five dollars damages for failure of defendant\u2019s passenger train to stop at a flag station and take the plaintiff on as a passenger, in response to his signal. Upon appeal, the Circuit Judge reversed the judgment, on the ground that there was no. evidence of either actual or punitive damages, upon which the judgment could be supported.\nIt is well established that this Court cannot review the Circuit Court\u2019s findings of fact in a case before that Court on appeal from a magistrate court.\nThe judgment of this Court is, that the judgment of the Circuit Court be affirmed.", "type": "majority", "author": "Mr. Justice Woods."}], "attorneys": ["Messrs. Moise & Clifton, for appellant. Messrs. Lee & Moise, contra."], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "JAMES v. NORTHWESTERN RAILROAD CO.\nMagistrate Court \u2014 Finding oe Fact. \u2014 This Court cannot review the findings of fact by Circuit Court on appeal from magistrate court.\nBefore Gary, J., Sumter, July, 1903.\nAffirmed.\nAction by Walter James against Northwestern Railroad Co. From Circuit order reversing judgment of magistrate court, plaintiff appeals.\nMessrs. Moise & Clifton, for appellant. Messrs. Lee & Moise, contra.\nMarch 4, 1905."}, "file_name": "0554-01", "first_page_order": 566, "last_page_order": 567}